# Always Use Quickmerge

RULE: ALWAYS run `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "message"`. NEVER run `scripts/quality-gates.sh` standalone. Use `--dep-branch` when dependencies differ from main. Branch protection rejects direct push to main.
WHY: Quickmerge runs dependency cascade, pre-flight audit, quality gates, Act simulation, and PR creation. Standalone quality gates miss critical checks.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/feature-branch-workflow.md, 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md

## Three-Tier Branch Model

```
feat/*   → QG only, no PR (feature iteration — auto-detected, no --no-pr needed)
staging  → convergence zone; breaking changes + SIT; auto-PR targets main after SIT
main     → always stable; NEVER a direct target for breaking changes
```

| Commit type | Target | Command |
|-------------|--------|---------|
| `fix:` / `feat:` / `chore:` | main (direct) | `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "fix: ..."` |
| `feat!:` / `BREAKING CHANGE:` | staging (via --to-staging) | `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat!: ..." --to-staging` |
| Feature iteration | no PR | auto when on `feat/*` branch |

**Hotfix path:** Non-breaking commits go directly to main. No staging gate needed.
**Breaking change path:** MUST use `--to-staging`. Cascade runs through staging. SIT validates. `staging-to-main.yml` merges to main automatically after SIT passes.
**Staging lock:** If `staging_status.locked = true` in `workspace-manifest.json`, `--to-staging` exits with queue message. Non-breaking quickmerge to main is NOT blocked.

## Dependency Cascade

- **Feature mode (--dep-branch):** cascades across dep repos on a named feature branch; QG only, no PR. Branch auto-derived from current git branch.
- **Staging mode (--to-staging):** cascades breaking change through ALL actual dependents (recursive DAG walk via `topologicalOrder`); PRs target staging. Branch auto-derived from HEAD.
- **`--branch NAME` + `--to-staging`** → hard fail (mutually exclusive).
- The cascade is **selective**: only repos with a dependency edge to the changed repo are touched. Not all 60 repos.

**SSOT:** `unified-trading-pm/codex/08-workflows/ci-cd-flow.md` (§ "Dependency promotion") + `codex/08-workflows/dependency-cascade.md`

## Agent Sessions — MANDATORY

RULE: Agents (Claude Code, CI agents, run-agent.sh) MUST pass `--agent` to quickmerge.

Two-pass model:
- **Pass 1** — full QG: `bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` or `run-all-quality-gates.sh` — tests, typecheck, lint, codex all run
- **Pass 2** — quickmerge: lightweight verify only — lint + format + typecheck + codex; tests already passed in pass 1

`--agent` = skip act + skip tests. Quickmerge becomes a fast format/lint gate before PR creation.

## Push before quickmerge (local commits)

Quickmerge **stashes uncommitted** changes before switching branches, then **stash pop** — that protects dirty trees, not
**commits that exist only locally**. Stage 5 may run `git checkout -B <branch> origin/<branch>`, which sets the branch tip
to match the remote; **unpushed commits** can stop being reachable from the branch name (still in reflog until GC).

**Do this:** If you (or a prior step) already ran `git commit` on `feat/your-branch` and did **not** push, run
`git push -u origin feat/your-branch` **before** quickmerge. **Or** use quickmerge as the primary commit path after Pass 1
QG so there are no orphan local-only commits.

**Agents:** Same rule — never run quickmerge on a branch that is ahead of `origin` with unpushed commits unless you push
first (or you intend only uncommitted work + quickmerge’s own commit).

```bash
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: ..." --agent                          # skip act + tests
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: ..." --agent --skip-typecheck         # also skip typecheck
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: ..." --agent --skip-tests             # redundant (--agent already skips tests)
```

User can harden by omitting `--agent` (full QG re-runs including tests + act). Use `--quick` for human shortcut (skips act only, tests still run).

## Key Flags

`--to-staging` (breaking change cascade) | `--no-pr` (QG only, auto on feat/*) | `--dep-branch "feat/X"` (feature cascade) | `--unit-only` | `--agent` (agent sessions — skip act) | `--quick` (human shortcut — skip act) | `--skip-tests` | `--files "a.py b.py"`

