## DO

```bash
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add ConfigReloader"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "fix: tier boundary" --dep-branch "feat/rollback"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "chore: cleanup" --no-pr
```

## NEVER

```bash
bash scripts/quality-gates.sh                   # standalone — misses dep validation + PR
git add -A && git commit && git push            # bypasses all quality gates
git reset --hard origin/main                    # FORBIDDEN — destroys local changes
Finish with uncommitted changes in any modified repo    # commit your OWN edits — see note below
```

"Finish with uncommitted changes" targets the agent's **own** edits — never abandon your work in a dirty tree. It does
**NOT** mean sweeping another agent's concurrent WIP into your `--files` list. If dep-repo working trees you don't own
are dirty, **STOP and report to the user** before quickmerge; do not auto-bundle them. See CLAUDE.md key-rules and
`SUB_AGENT_MANDATORY_RULES.md` (Quickmerge Safety) — "DO NOT autonomously run quickmerge when local dep repos are dirty".

## Nothing-to-Commit on Staging

`git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: promote feat/X to staging"` then `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "chore: promote feat/X to staging"`
